-DBGUI File separated with 4 files (excluding lib)
    Connection file: has the Connection class between DB and java
    DAO file: has all the java classes for DAO (Operations on DB seperated), inteface for the main DAO operations CRUD(Create, update, read, delete)
    Enum file: has all the Enum files
    Tables: has all the main tables (there are mutlitple ones excluded)

-i seperated the files because it was too crowded.
-when you make a class, make sure to put it in it's file, and put the keyword 'package file_name' so java doesn't lose the class. if you want to is a certin class that 
is in another file write import file_name.class_name so you can access it

-i tested few query (selectAll) and it works perfectly, but since i wanted to start on the main because i'm a bit confused on the DAO methods i wanted to give you this 
zip file to know how the things are arranged

-there is text file called SQL.txt. when testing the connection, you must has atleast MySQL. the SQL.txt file has the DB data, just import it on MySQL or HeidiSQL. make 
sure your username in MySQL/ HeidiSQL called root, and the passwords is empty to match the connection class implementation

-good luck! ^^